vmvga: env-gated frame inspector for debugging guest rendering

Nothing changes unless the variables are set.

  VMVGA_DUMP_DIR=<dir>     touch <dir>/trigger: the next present writes
                           level 0 of every render target as raw files
                           (sid<N>_fmt<F>_<W>x<H>_pitch<P>.raw), and the
                           following frame is logged to <dir>/frame.txt
                           (every draw: shaders, targets, textures, key
                           states, result; clears, copies, blits).
  VMVGA_DUMP_TEXTURES=1    also write CPU shadows of large textures.
  VMVGA_DUMP_PS=<id,...>   in the logged frame, snapshot the first draw of
                           each pixel shader: VS/PS bytecode, constants,
                           texture and render states, vertex layout,
                           vertex buffers, bound textures' shadows and
                           the colour targets read back right after it
                           (<dir>/draw_ps<id>/).
  VMVGA_DUMP_ALL_RT=1      snapshots read back every render target.
  VMVGA_LOG_VOLUME=1       log every volume-texture DMA/copy with the
                           reason when the DMA is rejected.

Failing draws are logged with their failure stage, and shader failures
(undefined id, DXVK create/bind/constants) get their own frame-log line;
shaders DXVK refuses are written as bad-vs<id>.bin / bad-ps<id>.bin.

  VMVGA_FPS=1              every 5 s: presents/s and draws/s, FIFO and
                           command-buffer traffic (SYNC writes, FIFO
                           passes, fences, IRQs, stalls, CB submit/done/
                           yield/IRQ).
  VMVGA_PROFILE_DIR=<dir>  touch <dir>/profile: sample QEMU's main thread
                           (instruction pointer + top-of-stack word) every
                           0.5 ms of its CPU time for 10 s, then write
                           samples.txt and maps.

Host side: tools/framedump2png.py, tools/d3d9-disasm.py and
tools/profile-report.py.

